WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.560
- How are you?
(audience applauding)

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:02.393
- I'm great!

00:00:02.393 --> 00:00:03.723
- You're great? Oh-

00:00:03.723 --> 00:00:04.580
- I'm great! It's good to be here.

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:06.220
- [Kelly] Oh my God!
Seeing you is reminding...

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.060
Okay, I can't remember what...

00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:10.024
I saw y'all play and it was in Nashville.

00:00:10.024 --> 00:00:10.857
- [Dan] Yeah, yeah.

00:00:10.857 --> 00:00:12.860
- And it was in the woods
and a singer owned it,

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:13.693
a country singer.

00:00:13.693 --> 00:00:14.680
It was in the woods, it was outside.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:15.513
I'm trying to remember.

00:00:15.513 --> 00:00:16.400
Does it start with an "f"?

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:17.756
- I was trying to think
of that venue, too,

00:00:17.756 --> 00:00:18.589
but yeah, I don't remember.

00:00:18.589 --> 00:00:19.970
- [Kelly] The name of the
venue, it's such a random venue

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:20.930
in Nashville.

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:21.763
- It's beautiful, it was outside, yeah.

00:00:21.763 --> 00:00:22.600
- I know! That's what I'm saying!

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.150
I was trying to remember what it was,

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.190
'cause it was the coolest
place to see a concert, one,

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:27.620
and y'all killed it!

00:00:27.620 --> 00:00:28.453
- Thank you.

00:00:28.453 --> 00:00:29.740
- Anyway, I love seeing you live.

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:33.080
It's incredible to see someone
live that sounds even better.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:33.913
(Dan chuckles)

00:00:33.913 --> 00:00:35.789
You sound even better than
your records. It's rare.

00:00:35.789 --> 00:00:36.622
- Thank you, thank you.
(audience applauding)

00:00:36.622 --> 00:00:37.455
Appreciate that.

00:00:37.455 --> 00:00:38.966
- Anyway, have y'all met before?

00:00:38.966 --> 00:00:40.770
- Yes, we have.
- Yeah, oh yeah, yeah.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.392
We go way back.
- Yeah, we go way back.

00:00:42.392 --> 00:00:43.880
- Aw, bromance!
(audience laughs)

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:45.040
- Yeah.
- Yeah. Wow, your shoes!

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.189
It's crazy!
- Oh, you like 'em?

00:00:46.189 --> 00:00:47.022
You like' em?
(Kelly laughs)

00:00:47.022 --> 00:00:47.855
(audience laughs)
- [Dan] Wow!

00:00:47.855 --> 00:00:48.710
- [Shaq] Nice, right?
- [Dan] They look amaz...

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:49.543
What size is that?

00:00:49.543 --> 00:00:51.188
- 22.
(audience gasps)

00:00:51.188 --> 00:00:52.271
- What?
- Yes.

00:00:53.217 --> 00:00:54.888
- I never knew that was a shoe size!

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:55.721
- It is.

00:00:55.721 --> 00:00:57.693
- Just for you?
(audience laughs)

00:00:57.693 --> 00:00:59.480
Do other people have that size?

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:01.318
- Yes, they do.
- Oh my God!

00:01:01.318 --> 00:01:03.415
(Shaq laughs)
That's a big shoe, okay!

00:01:03.415 --> 00:01:04.423
(Shaq laughs)
(audience laughs)

00:01:04.423 --> 00:01:07.003
Well, there's no segway
there, just a lot of jokes.

00:01:07.003 --> 00:01:08.570
(audience laughs)

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:11.430
You've got four kids at
home, that's a lot of kiddos.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:13.150
So do they enjoy hearing dad play music?

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:15.290
Do they think you're cool still?

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:16.950
- I think they think I'm cool.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.670
I play music for them everyday.

00:01:18.670 --> 00:01:22.153
I write everyday and
between them and my wife,

00:01:23.247 --> 00:01:24.930
they're the ones who pick what goes on

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:26.200
an Imagine Dragons record.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.040
I play them the songs, and
if they wanna hear it again,

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:30.970
then I'm like, "Okay,
there's something here."

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:31.931
- [Kelly] Wow.
- And if they don't,

00:01:31.931 --> 00:01:33.940
then it doesn't make the record.

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:36.241
So you can thank my four year
olds for putting it together.

00:01:36.241 --> 00:01:37.077
(audience applauds)
- They have great taste!

00:01:37.077 --> 00:01:38.690
- Yeah, so they hear the records, yes.

00:01:38.690 --> 00:01:39.523
- They have great taste.

00:01:39.523 --> 00:01:43.430
So Shaq, your kids like to rap
and DJ with you, don't they?

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:44.380
- Yes, they do.
- Yeah?

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:45.829
Are they good at it?

00:01:45.829 --> 00:01:46.998
- They're pretty good.

00:01:46.998 --> 00:01:48.660
- They're...
(Kelly laughs and claps)

00:01:48.660 --> 00:01:50.359
He's like, "Not as good as me."

00:01:50.359 --> 00:01:52.370
(audience cheers)

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:54.430
- [Shaq] This is during the pandemic

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:56.590
and we all had to stay in the house, so-

00:01:56.590 --> 00:01:57.680
- That is...

00:01:57.680 --> 00:01:59.840
First of all, you had the best pandemic

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:01.870
family thing happening.

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:04.630
Nobody was having that kind
of fun during the pandemic.

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:05.830
That's amazing!
(audience laughing)

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:08.160
Well, Dan, I've heard this
new album was a tough one

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:08.993
to work on.

00:02:08.993 --> 00:02:10.430
Why?

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:12.440
- Well, first of all,
Rick Rubin produced it,

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:14.956
who's a legend in himself.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:14.956 --> 00:02:15.956
(audience applauds)

00:02:15.956 --> 00:02:17.742
And when you're sitting down with... Yeah.

00:02:17.742 --> 00:02:18.960
- You feel intimidated?
- Well, yeah. I mean it's-

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:20.340
- "I gotta bring my A game"?

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:22.800
- Well, I already...

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.610
I've never gone over
my lyrics with anybody.

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:26.760
I've always self-produced
for the most part,

00:02:26.760 --> 00:02:28.860
and I always write all
the lyrics and melody,

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:30.120
and sitting down with Rick Rubin,

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.790
he wanted to go over every lyric

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:33.040
and would question me about it.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.210
Like, "Why did you say this about that?

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:36.220
Do you really feel that way?"

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:38.147
- Oh, now that gives me a panic attack.

00:02:38.147 --> 00:02:39.793
- I'm just like, "Oh, gosh!"
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:39.793 --> 00:02:41.290
I wanna hide and it's Rick Rubin,

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:43.870
and his beard, and he's like, "Well"...

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:45.147
And he would say things like,

00:02:45.147 --> 00:02:45.980
"You know,

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:48.670
that line feels like you're
not really being honest."

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:50.678
- [Kelly] Oh my God, it's like therapy!

00:02:50.678 --> 00:02:51.840
(Dan laughs)
- I'm like, "Oh!"

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:53.930
- That's like my therapist calling me out.

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:55.979
I'll be like, "Oh my God,
bad connection! I can't..."

00:02:55.979 --> 00:02:57.847
(audience laughs)
All of a sudden the Zoom ends.

00:02:57.847 --> 00:03:00.180
(Kelly laughs)
- But, that being said,

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.110
it was great, it's what
I wanted on this record.

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:03.060
I wanted someone to push me,

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:05.736
so between Rick and Shaq
being in the studio with me,

00:03:05.736 --> 00:03:06.569
(Kelly and audience laughs)

00:03:06.569 --> 00:03:08.152
it pushed me.
- You're two friends!

00:03:08.152 --> 00:03:10.782
- [Dan] My two friends!
(indistinct)

00:03:10.782 --> 00:03:11.774
- You have amazing friends!

00:03:11.774 --> 00:03:13.000
- That'd be really cool
if my best friends were

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:13.921
Rick Rubin and Shaq since I was 12.

00:03:13.921 --> 00:03:14.910
(Kelly laughs and claps)

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:16.020
- [Kelly] That's amazing!

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.710
That would give me a panic
attack being in a room

00:03:17.710 --> 00:03:19.800
and someone questioning
every lyric that I'd wrote.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:20.945
- Yeah, it was tough.
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:03:20.945 --> 00:03:22.050
- But it was great.

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:22.883
It's our fifth record,

00:03:22.883 --> 00:03:24.898
I wanted someone to push me
like that, so, it helped.

00:03:24.898 --> 00:03:26.000
- Oh!

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:28.138
Oh, and look, it just appeared!

00:03:28.138 --> 00:03:30.090
(Kelly laughs)
(audience and Shaq laughs)

00:03:30.090 --> 00:03:31.083
Thank you, Justin!

00:03:31.930 --> 00:03:32.770
I love this!
- [Dan] Thank you.

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:35.570
I love all the art that always
comes with your albums, too.

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:36.740
I think it's so cool.

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:39.330
And you've also started
up a special charity.

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:40.680
Can you explain what it is?

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:41.870
- Yeah, it's LOVELOUD.

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:43.850
It's in Utah, is where it started,

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:45.100
and we wanna bring it to other places,

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:47.280
but it's really just focused
on igniting the conversation

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:50.430
about what it means to love and celebrate

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.163
your LGBTQ children.

00:03:53.190 --> 00:03:55.690
When a child is raised, especially
in a religious community

00:03:55.690 --> 00:04:00.130
and they're LGBTQ, their
suicide rate skyrockets.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.930
The depression, anxiety rates skyrocket,

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:04.130
so it's really about
changing the conversation,

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:06.027
igniting these conversations
with these families about,

00:04:06.027 --> 00:04:07.820
"Hey, how do we celebrate our children?"

00:04:07.820 --> 00:04:08.653
I really don't like...

00:04:08.653 --> 00:04:10.310
The term "accept" kind of feels like,

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:12.760
it's like, "I'll accept you."

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.880
But "celebrate" is really
the word we try to use,

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:18.630
which is like, "How do we
let our LGBTQ children know

00:04:18.630 --> 00:04:20.570
they're perfect just the way they are?"

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:22.050
And they deserve to be celebrated,

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:24.070
and especially in these
religious communities,

00:04:24.070 --> 00:04:26.030
let's have these uncomfortable,
hard conversations

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:27.750
and help the parents know that,

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:29.620
there's really only one choice
and that's to let your child

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:32.408
be who they need to be, love
them, and celebrate them.

00:04:32.408 --> 00:04:33.241
(audience cheers)
That's what LOVELOUD is.

00:04:33.241 --> 00:04:34.752
- Yeah, love their story.

00:04:34.752 --> 00:04:37.360
It's so crazy, we all have kids.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:38.883
It's crazy to me.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:44.030
I'm just hopeful that my kids find love.

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:46.190
I don't care who it's with,
you know what I'm saying?

00:04:46.190 --> 00:04:47.023
- Right.

00:04:47.023 --> 00:04:50.080
- If you find love, real
love, authentic love,

00:04:50.080 --> 00:04:51.840
hold on with both hands.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:52.673
I'm gonna tell my...

00:04:52.673 --> 00:04:54.380
Regardless of who you're into.

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:55.213
- [Dan] For sure.
- I just think,

00:04:55.213 --> 00:04:58.480
well, if you find that,
count yourself so lucky.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.700
It's funny that we worry
about all the other stuff

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.090
when really it is just that fundamental.

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:02.960
We all wanna be loved.
- [Dan] Yeah.

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:06.290
- We wanna be respected,
we wanna be successful,

00:05:06.290 --> 00:05:07.123
all those things.

00:05:07.123 --> 00:05:08.803
It's so funny how we complicate it.

